  "live_records": {
    "q-169189": {
      "dom_id": "step-q169189",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14193755/assets/b7d373c510472102242794bc21b60a6e0c12100213c6e01aac640feb398fc573.png)\n\nWhich of the shapes above is **NOT** a regular polygon?",
      "worked_solution": "A regular polygon is a polygon that has the following properties:\n\n- All sides have the same length (i.e., congruent).\n\n- All angles have the same measure (i.e., congruent).\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each polygon in turn:\n\n- Polygon I is regular. Its sides and angles are all congruent.\n\n- Polygon II is *not* regular. Its sides and angles are *not* all congruent.\n\n- Polygon III is regular. Its sides and angles are all congruent.\n\nTherefore the answer is \"II only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
