    "q-67891": {
      "dom_id": "step-q67891",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14193755/assets/e17bf0ffc492fc1ed22d97e422cf9926bfac01ac765614bbe63b887853d65e2e.png)\n\nDetermine the measure of each interior angle of a regular octagon.",
      "worked_solution": "A regular octagon is an $8$-sided polygon where all the interior angles have the same measure.\n\nThe sum of the measures of its interior angles is \n\n$$\n{180}^{∘}\\times (8-2)=1\\,{080}^{∘}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the measure of each interior angle is \n\n$$\n\\frac{1\\,{080}^{∘}}{8}={135}^{∘}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
