    "q-67902": {
      "dom_id": "step-q67902",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "In a regular polygon, all the exterior angles have a measure of ${30}^{∘}.$ How many sides does the polygon have?",
      "worked_solution": "The sum of the exterior angles of any polygon is ${360}^{∘}.$ \n\nFor a regular polygon, all exterior angles have the same measure. \n\nTherefore, the number of exterior angles is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{360}^{∘}}{{30}^{∘}}=12\\,.\n$$\n\nThe number of sides, then, is also $12.$",
