      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14193755/assets/0425d0fe9dea48f907b945e659ec94311bdc868a3ede3c484c6b1ed6fc6f3b9f.png)\n\nWhat is the measure of each exterior angle of a regular nonagon?",
      "worked_solution": "For any polygon, the exterior angles sum to ${360}^{∘}.$ In a regular nonagon, there are $9$ equivalent exterior angles, so each has a measure of \n\n$$\n\\frac{{360}^{∘}}{9}={40}^{∘}.\n$$",
